msgid "Two open pull requests that share a head repository *and* a head branch, to different bases, cannot be told apart from the run payload: the runs of a fork PR carry an empty `pull_requests` array, the same `head_branch` and the same `head_sha`. The helper therefore asks the API whether any other open pull request shares that head, and drops the branch matcher while one does — cancelling nothing beats cancelling the wrong pull request. If that lookup itself fails the matcher stays on, because a failed lookup is far more likely than a shared head."
